WEBVTT

00:00:01,390 --> 00:00:09,710
Hello, Dr. Kevin Cutters again here just sharing some of your most frequently asked questions.

00:00:09,710 --> 00:00:10,870
Here's one.

00:00:10,870 --> 00:00:14,910
What do I do when I get other testing done?

00:00:14,910 --> 00:00:19,170
Maybe you get it done at your functional medicine doctor locally.

00:00:19,170 --> 00:00:21,470
Maybe you got it done at your oncologist.

00:00:21,470 --> 00:00:29,470
Maybe you had your natural path out of the street do a lab or something like that.

00:00:29,470 --> 00:00:35,370
So we're talking about testing that you got done that we did in order that our clinic did

00:00:35,370 --> 00:00:36,370
in order.

00:00:36,370 --> 00:00:37,370
You got something done.

00:00:37,370 --> 00:00:45,150
You had an exam, let's say at your oncologist office, you met with a surgeon, something like

00:00:45,150 --> 00:00:47,310
that and they gave you information.

00:00:47,310 --> 00:00:54,150
So you have labs, you have CT scans, you have PET scans, MRIs, some other data that you want

00:00:54,150 --> 00:00:56,830
to share with us.

00:00:56,830 --> 00:01:07,390
This is where it goes, send it to labs, L-A-B-S, at cuttersclinic.com, labs at cuttersclinic.com.

00:01:07,390 --> 00:01:08,390
That comes to us.

00:01:08,390 --> 00:01:16,470
It comes in an email so that we can then put that, please put it in a PDF form if at all possible

00:01:16,470 --> 00:01:21,230
and then in that PDF that we can upload it into your file.

00:01:21,230 --> 00:01:24,030
So that's how we get it into your file.

00:01:24,030 --> 00:01:33,470
Now understand when you send us a lab or data or something that you had done or if you

00:01:33,470 --> 00:01:38,430
have a concern with that, the impetus is on you to contact us.

00:01:38,430 --> 00:01:43,830
So you're just sending us your information that is done in an outside source.

00:01:43,830 --> 00:01:49,950
So we're not going to make an assumption that you want to talk about it.

00:01:49,950 --> 00:01:56,510
So when we look at that email, that's going to be taken care of by an employee of mine.

00:01:56,510 --> 00:01:58,470
So they're not going to connect with you.

00:01:58,470 --> 00:02:05,190
If you want to go over that data in any way possible, we're happy to do so.

00:02:05,190 --> 00:02:11,230
Contact our office, call the clinic and make an appointment with myself or Michelle or

00:02:11,230 --> 00:02:12,750
your liaison.

00:02:12,750 --> 00:02:16,910
If you just need to talk about it, if there's something you don't understand, many times

00:02:16,910 --> 00:02:23,910
we understand other practitioners don't have the time or they're just not set up in a

00:02:23,910 --> 00:02:27,390
way to really explain a lab or a test to you.

00:02:27,390 --> 00:02:31,990
They might just kind of cursly go over, well, it's worse we need to do this or it's better

00:02:31,990 --> 00:02:36,510
we need to do this and you just maybe you want some understanding about it, we're happy

00:02:36,510 --> 00:02:37,510
to do that.

00:02:37,510 --> 00:02:42,230
Understand there's going to be a fee for that for you to spend time with us to do that.

00:02:42,230 --> 00:02:47,750
So we're happy to do that to explain to the best of our knowledge what that data that

00:02:47,750 --> 00:02:49,390
you're setting us means.

00:02:49,390 --> 00:02:56,990
So just understand you'll just pay per visit and per 15 minutes slot like any other visit

00:02:56,990 --> 00:03:01,910
you would have to pay for, but we're here to go over your concerns.

00:03:01,910 --> 00:03:08,230
If the test is better and you want to celebrate, call us and celebrate and that's great.

00:03:08,230 --> 00:03:09,910
We'd love to hear from you.

00:03:09,910 --> 00:03:15,750
If it's worse and you need some concern, you need some understanding or we need to ask

00:03:15,750 --> 00:03:21,190
to be retested, this is a good time to maybe do a cheek swab, this is a good time to maybe

00:03:21,190 --> 00:03:27,750
tweak your frequencies, do everything that we can do our part, which has to do with your

00:03:27,750 --> 00:03:34,510
nutrition and your diet and your frequencies or anything that we can recommend on our part.

00:03:34,510 --> 00:03:38,670
Or if you just need some help to go over whether you should do keyboard things, we're always

00:03:38,670 --> 00:03:43,270
happy to talk to you, but you have to call and make that appointment.

00:03:43,270 --> 00:03:45,350
I can't read your mind.

00:03:45,350 --> 00:03:47,590
So don't ask me to do that.

00:03:47,590 --> 00:03:51,350
So don't get mad at me if we didn't contact you.

00:03:51,350 --> 00:03:56,950
We're here for you to reach out, we're here five days a week, you can call and make an appointment.

00:03:56,950 --> 00:04:02,670
So we're here for you to talk about things, we're here for you to bounce ideas off.

00:04:02,670 --> 00:04:05,790
This is what my oncologist said, what do you think about that?

00:04:05,790 --> 00:04:10,190
We're here to retest you, we're here to tweak some things on our side and mostly we're

00:04:10,190 --> 00:04:13,350
here to pray for you and pray with you.

00:04:13,350 --> 00:04:20,230
So we want to be that support in that way for you as best as we possibly can.

00:04:20,230 --> 00:04:25,790
So utilize us, we're your friend, we're your companion, we're not your dictator.

00:04:25,790 --> 00:04:30,670
So we're your coach to help guide you, we're not your boss.

00:04:30,670 --> 00:04:36,110
So that's the difference in our clinic and some of the other clinics out there.

00:04:36,110 --> 00:04:43,390
So utilize us in that way and we will have a great relationship.

00:04:43,390 --> 00:04:47,630
No no matter what you do, we'll be praying for you in all things.

00:04:47,630 --> 00:04:55,390
Remember that's labs at codersclinic.com, labs at codersclinic.com.

00:04:55,390 --> 00:04:56,190
